# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 🔐 Ignore sensitive, system-specific, or temp files
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SSH and secrets
ssh/config.private
*.key
*.pem
*.gpg
*.env
.env.*
*.secrets
*.token

# Temporary / backup files
*~
*.sw?
*.tmp
*.bak
*.old
*.orig

# Logs
*.log

# macOS system files
.DS_Store
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
__MACOSX/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Python (the repo ships one script; py_compile drops this next to it)
__pycache__/

# IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.sublime-*
*.iml

# Claude Code local settings (repo-specific)
.claude/

# ...but this repo's own CLAUDE.md is tracked on purpose. A rule in
# ~/.config/git/ignore excludes CLAUDE.md from every repo, which is the right default
# for client work and the wrong one here: the trigger map that keeps this repo's docs
# honest is useless if it does not travel with the repo. A pattern in a .gitignore
# outranks one in core.excludesFile, so this negation is what makes it trackable.
!CLAUDE.md
